#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a9d88d-8478-534d-b20a-f7e25d74ee09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+10}{s^2-2s+7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a9d88d-8478-534d-b20a-f7e25d74ee09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+10}{s^2-2s+7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544093} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1988ed4-093d-51e3-9639-cb7ca3f1716c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4b0fddb-f441-5332-9904-2f366a824fe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-331950" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)=2 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]-3{X}_{2}(s) & =2 \\\\ 4(s-1)-(s-1)^{2}{X}_{2}(s)-6{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 4(s-1)-[(s-1)^{2}+6]{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 4(s-1)-({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =4-4(s-1) \\\\ -({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =-4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-(s-1)\\cdot \\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}-2s+7)-(s-1)\\cdot 4(s-2)}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-8s+28-4(s-1)(s-2)}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s+20}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(s+5)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(s+5)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d461234f-027a-557e-9d34-651597fcb58b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d461234f-027a-557e-9d34-651597fcb58b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544537} :answer-field/id #uuid "337fbbd0-2104-528d-b75a-5b62951f2ab9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "229cdf1d-b683-5de3-b351-27b1d6a26233" :question/math-academy-id "q-332026" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-3){X}_{2}(s)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]+3{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ (s-2)[-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)]+6{X}_{2}(s) & =8 \\\\ -2(s-2)-[(s-2)(s-3)-6]{X}_{2}(s) & =8 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s){X}_{2}(s) & =8+2(s-2) \\\\ -s(s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2s+4 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-(s-3)\\cdot \\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2s(s+5)+2(s-3)(s+2)}{2s(s-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6acad7a-a7d5-50fe-94f8-03cc12e4ce79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6acad7a-a7d5-50fe-94f8-03cc12e4ce79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544448} :answer-field/id #uuid "0abaee99-8d00-5498-8655-f03c7de5849a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "357de87f-e9e1-5bed-9740-cf1a1c066776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "357de87f-e9e1-5bed-9740-cf1a1c066776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544205} :answer-field/id #uuid "43cb3dab-7c67-5df5-bb7f-1b8561a9585b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ba96b2e-684a-5f93-b08a-1f0e2229610c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ba96b2e-684a-5f93-b08a-1f0e2229610c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544324} :answer-field/id #uuid "67bc3df3-21d6-5ff8-936a-39854725ffb5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0a2880-de85-52e8-85de-0969492cdb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c0a2880-de85-52e8-85de-0969492cdb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544217} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0f9134-af7b-577f-bb8b-2009b066b22f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0737b10-0304-5e2e-a18d-ef1cf02a07ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-332382" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3{e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad88c67b-7dd2-5b78-a6b2-b39c461d1394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad88c67b-7dd2-5b78-a6b2-b39c461d1394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544457} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dec9ee2-df88-5435-a628-2db834f23d11" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fdf95821-0667-5470-9d72-b2c2cd72e470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdf95821-0667-5470-9d72-b2c2cd72e470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544642} :answer-field/id #uuid "43acf565-70e8-59c8-9da0-7f2d6c9509f6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa7dfaa-3002-551e-b29b-b70703cbc0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fa7dfaa-3002-551e-b29b-b70703cbc0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544433} :answer-field/id #uuid "62b0c5b0-195a-52a8-a42e-0d7cdd505876" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86aa83a1-0b94-57bd-b3df-ddec044a5317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86aa83a1-0b94-57bd-b3df-ddec044a5317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544378} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8e0339e-584d-50e3-9d66-c4b5654e80f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9de0e52e-4e54-5cd5-8e58-4fda732ef76e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332388" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{5t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2\\cdot t}+{e}^{5\\cdot t} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2t}+{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{2t}+{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7d556d2-a534-5571-b90c-4c9a7094d56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7d556d2-a534-5571-b90c-4c9a7094d56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303593} :answer-field/id #uuid "077f3dec-5492-5a4a-b6aa-6bc350e5c436" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4a0338-aef3-5c56-93c6-e236ce9d4afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4a0338-aef3-5c56-93c6-e236ce9d4afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303249} :answer-field/id #uuid "986e6b38-dcdd-578a-b434-9a00e0d1fb85" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdee0a55-3096-5aa4-af6d-3d685b5431de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdee0a55-3096-5aa4-af6d-3d685b5431de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303729} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0af3812-c6d0-5b42-895f-770d6db05863" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ecc283f-a6e2-5680-818e-066fc64745c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ecc283f-a6e2-5680-818e-066fc64745c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303134} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ab0df7-f64e-5225-a2be-146b547645a3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11bc6671-f60f-5e8a-924a-ddb4eef9ace3" :question/math-academy-id "q-332436" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{4}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 4-{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
